                "senderName": "NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued November 4 at 4:50PM CST until November 7 at 6:00AM CST by NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nLouisiana...\n\nCalcasieu River near White Oak Park affecting Calcasieu Parish.\n\nFor the Calcasieu River...including Glenmora, Oakdale, Oberlin,\nKinder, White Oak Park, Salt Water Barrier...Minor flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Calcasieu River near White Oak Park.\n\n* WHEN...Until Saturday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 2.0 feet, Minor flooding of Goos Ferry Road will\noccur.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 4:35 PM CST Wednesday the stage was 1.6 feet.\n- Forecast...The river will oscillate around flood stage with a\nmaximum value of 2.1 feet tomorrow evening.\n- Flood stage is 2.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.",
